# Diagram Index Schema
#
# Path: .loom/diagrams/index.toon
# Producer: /loom-diagram (skills/loom-diagram/SKILL.md) — appends one row
#           per generated triplet (<slug>.md + <slug>.excalidraw + <slug>.svg)
# Consumers:
#   - /loom-docs release (skills/loom-docs-release) — drift detection: if the
#     SHA of the .md source differs from the recorded shaShort but the
#     rendered .excalidraw / .svg files predate the last edit, the release
#     gate reports DIAGRAM_DRIFT_DETECTED (see protocols/exit-codes.md)
#
# Rules:
#   - Append-only registry of generated diagram triplets
#   - Writes are atomic: write to {path}.tmp then fs.renameSync
#   - path is the triplet base path WITHOUT extension; the three artifacts
#     live at {path}.md, {path}.excalidraw, {path}.svg (plus .png when a
#     rasterizer is available)
#   - schemaVersion bumped on any breaking field change
#
# Field descriptions:
#   slug         string  diagram identifier derived from the input file
#                        basename or the first noun-phrase of --prose
#   path         string  triplet base path relative to the repo root, e.g.
#                        docs/diagrams/login-flow
#   source       enum    invocation mode the .md source holds: prose | mermaid
#   generatedAt  string  ISO 8601 timestamp of triplet generation
#   shaShort     string  truncated SHA-256 of the .md source at generation
#                        time — the drift-detection anchor

schemaVersion: 1

diagrams[N]{slug,path,source,generatedAt,shaShort}:
  login-flow,docs/diagrams/login-flow,mermaid,2026-06-30T17:50:00Z,a1b2c3d
